# Client source material — see input/README.md
#
# Text, notes, and small images under input/ are committed: provenance should travel with
# the repo. Large or confidential binaries are not. When you exclude one, commit a stub
# beside it (`<name>.<ext>.txt`) naming the file and where it actually lives — a missing
# file that nothing points at is indistinguishable from a file that never existed.

input/**/*.pdf
input/**/*.mp4
input/**/*.mov
input/**/*.wav
input/**/*.m4a
input/**/*.zip

# Stubs are the whole point — always keep them.
!input/**/*.txt

# External reference standards (specs are large and usually redistribution-restricted).
# Same stub rule applies: keep a .txt naming the document and where to obtain it.
context/files/*
!context/files/*.txt
!context/files/README.md

# Diagram exports. Renders of the repo-wide diagrams (ERD, class, component) are regenerated on
# demand and never tracked, along with every debug crop (see the mandatory export-and-verify
# loop in drawio-general-guide.md). Sequence-diagram renders are the exception: they live in
# pm/issues/<issue>/ and ARE committed; see the note further down.
*.drawio.png
**/examples/**/*.png
# The ERD, class and component renders live here beside their sources and stay untracked —
# they are cited repo-wide and regenerated on demand. Only sequence-diagram renders move out,
# to pm/issues/<issue>/, where they are committed (drawio-general-guide.md, amended 2026-08-21).
# A seq-uc*.png left in this directory is a stray duplicate — delete it, don't commit it.
docs/diagrams/*.png

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
